{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Progress 2026-11-11 PST: claimed (cert current, verified via review-plan --status from a worktree at origin/main b878c4be768). Implemented in worktree engine-switch, local commit d5bb898ab6b; make verify next, then Gerrit push.\n\nOne deviation from the plan text, needed to meet AC2 (zero LLM calls under \"agentic\"): besides the 3 pipeline-only shortcuts, the post-dispatch tail (rising/completion/drift floors, xcheck, fix-unit grouping) also makes LLM sub-calls. Measured: with a drift-stale attestation, drift_floor.maybe_apply ran a novelty call on the degraded agentic INDETERMINATE. That tail is extracted into _apply_review_floors and skipped when engine != \"pipeline\" and the verdict is llm_unavailable (the failed agentic run); a floor short-circuit still gets the identical tail under both engines. _run_plan_review complexity 18 (ceiling 19), __init__.py 695 LOC.\n\nTest note: a DET verdict with 2+ blockers makes the pre-existing fix-unit grouping call under BOTH engines (identical); the floor-blocked test uses a single-blocker plan so its zero-call assertion holds."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794424582842104151,"uuid":"5743098c-3867-420c-b43a-d00513a69847"}